    [Doc] Remove obsolete MTP deployment examples from DeepSeek-V4-Flash tutorial (#20323)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Remove the four obsolete A2/A3 MTP deployment tabs from Sections 5.1 and
    5.2 of the DeepSeek-V4-Flash tutorial. Keep the existing DSpark examples
    and rename their tabs to `A2 series` / `A3 series`.
    
    Remove stale MTP weight, image, model-path and comparison references,
    and repair links to the retained examples. Preserve main's DSpark launch
    parameters, the FAQ's MTP layers information, and all accuracy results.
    No shared PD parameter guidance is added or expanded.
    
    This applies the release documentation cleanup to main.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime behavior changes; documentation only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Repository markdownlint and codespell hooks passed for the changed
    tutorial.
    - `git diff --check` passed.
    - Parsed the rendered Markdown: four tab groups and 51 code blocks; no
    broken internal anchors.
    - Compared retained DSpark tabs with the original main version: launch
    parameters unchanged, apart from replacing the stale MTP model path in
    the A2 single-node example. Accuracy and FAQ content is unchanged.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci`; stopped after it stalled while
    installing the actionlint Go environment. Full repository checks remain
    for CI.
    - No NPU runtime tests: this change only removes obsolete documentation
    and preserves the retained deployment parameters.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    Documentation-only change; code boundary, regression, failure-path and
    performance tests are not applicable.
    
